0100:     Rule
0101:     - Redraw every object on an empty background canvas without changing its color, shape, or horizontal position.
0102:     - Closed frame objects slide vertically upward to the first non-colliding position.
0103:     - Open objects slide vertically downward to the first non-colliding position.
0104:     - Within each direction, preserve the original vertical order so overlapping columns stack instead of crossing.
0105: 
0106:     Key insight
0107:     - The only role distinction is whether an object encloses a hole: hole objects pack against the top edge, while non-hole objects pack against the bottom edge.
0108:     """
0109:     g = np.asarray(grid, dtype=int)
