0016:     """Erase the control bars and tile each matched sprite toward its bar.
0017: 
0018:     Input structure
0019:     - The background contains colored non-line sprites plus one-cell-thick control
0020:       bars.
0021:     - A horizontal bar has the same column span as a sprite; a vertical bar has
0022:       the same row span as a sprite.
0023: 
0024:     Rule
0025:     - Remove every control bar.
0026:     - For each bar, find the nearest sprite aligned with the bar's span on the
0027:       perpendicular axis.
0028:     - Repeat that sprite periodically from its original position toward the bar,
0029:       clipping at the grid boundary and leaving sprite-background cells empty.
0030: 
0031:     Key insight
0032:     - The bar is not copied itself; it gives the direction and terminal line for
0033:       repeating the aligned sprite motif.
0034:     """
0035:     g = np.asarray(grid, dtype=int)
0036:     bg = get_bg(g)
0037:     components = find_components(g, bg=bg, connectivity=4, monochromatic=True)
0038: 
0039:     sprites = []
0040:     bars = []
0041:     for component in components:
0042:         r0, c0, r1, c1 = component["bbox"]
0043:         height = r1 - r0 + 1
0044:         width = c1 - c0 + 1
0045:         if (height == 1) ^ (width == 1):
0046:             assert component["area"] == height * width
0047:             bars.append(component)
0048:         else:
0049:             assert height > 1 and width > 1
0050:             sprites.append(component)
